    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All 62 tests pass \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`, no regressions.\n\n## What I implemented\n\nThe `POST /api/owners` endpoint now honors an optional `Idempotency-Key` header: a repeat create with an already-seen key returns the originally created owner with **200**, instead of making a duplicate (which the identity check would otherwise reject with 409).\n\n**Three new function classes** (in `rest/function/owner/`):\n\n- **`IdempotencyStore`** \u2014 a `@Component` process-wide `ConcurrentHashMap<String, Integer>` mapping key \u2192 owner id.\n- **`CheckIdempotencyKey`** \u2014 new pipeline entry point. Reads the header from the injected `ServerHttpConnection`; on a recorded key it loads the original owner and responds 200 with the `OwnerDto`, short-circuiting the pipeline. Otherwise it triggers the `@Flow(\"proceed\")` branch to run the normal create pipeline.\n- **`RegisterIdempotency`** \u2014 runs right after `SaveOwner` (id now assigned), recording the key against the new owner id.\n\n**YAML wiring** (`officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`):\n- Added `idempotency` as the first step with `outputs: { proceed: validate }`, so the normal path is unchanged and the cache-hit path skips all validation/quota/duplicate rules.\n- Inserted `register` between `save` and `audit`.\n\nDesign notes:\n- The key is read directly from the HTTP request headers (metadata, safe to read twice) rather than routed through a shared variable, avoiding any `@Val`/type-collision concerns.\n- The cache-hit lookup uses the existing `findById` (which `left join fetch`es pets, so no lazy-loading issue) and falls through to a fresh create if the recorded owner is gone (`DataAccessException`) \u2014 robust against a rolled-back or deleted owner.\n- Both new steps carry `govern: [ transaction ]`, consistent with the rest of the pipeline.",
