    "probe_text": "Done \u2014 I read the `owners.POST.yml` pipeline and every function class it invokes (plus the helpers). Here is the complete ordered list of what happens on `POST /api/owners`.\n\n## Preconditions (whole endpoint)\n\n- **Authorization** \u2014 the file is guarded by `authorize: \"hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')\"`, so a caller without that role is rejected (403) before any step runs.\n- **Transaction governance** \u2014 every step carries `govern: [ transaction ]`, so the whole pipeline runs in one transaction and commits once at the end; any escalation rolls it back.\n\n## The pipeline, in order\n\n**1. `CheckIdempotencyKey`** \u2014 reads the optional `Idempotency-Key` header. If that key was already recorded for a completed create *and* the referenced owner still exists, it **short-circuits**: responds **200** with the originally-created owner and runs none of the steps below (no duplicate, no quota/duplicate rules). Otherwise it takes the `proceed` branch.\n\n**2. `ValidateOwnerFields`** (the one step that binds `@RequestBody`):\n- *Validation* \u2014 requires non-blank `firstName`, `lastName`, `city`, `telephone`, and an address in **either** structured (`addressLine1`) **or** flat (`address`) form. Every missing/blank field is collected and thrown together as **400** (`OwnerFieldsInvalidException` listing all offenders).\n- *Validation* \u2014 a supplied `registrationDate` in the future is added to that 400 error list.\n- *Side-effect* \u2014 normalizes the address (trim/collapse whitespace, upper-case, expand `ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE`); composes structured lines into `address` and sets/clears `addressLine1/2`; writes back.\n- *Validation + side-effect* \u2014 normalizes `telephone` to E.164 (keeps explicit `+`/country code, else assumes `+61` and drops a leading `0`; enforces 8\u201315 digits and country-specific national length); **400** (`telephone`) if it can't form a valid number; writes the normalized value back.\n- *Validation + side-effect* \u2014 if `email` is present, it must match the syntactic regex (**400** `email`), is lower-cased, and is rejected (**400** `email`) if its domain is disposable (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`); writes back.\n- Publishes the normalized body for later steps.\n\n**3. `ValidatePostcode`** \u2014 *validation only*, `postcode` optional. When present it must be exactly 4 digits (**400**), and if the city maps to a known region (Sydney\u2192NSW 2000\u20132099, Melbourne\u2192VIC 3000\u20133099, Brisbane\u2192QLD 4000\u20134099) it must fall inside that range (**400**). Unknown city \u2192 any 4 digits accepted.\n\n**4. `CheckOwnerCityCapacity`** \u2014 *validation*: **409** if the city already holds \u2265 50 owners (case-insensitive match).\n\n**5. `CheckOwnerDailyCreateLimit`** \u2014 *validation*: **429** if \u2265 100 existing owners have a `registrationDate` equal to today's business day (weekend/holiday rolled forward).\n\n**6. `BuildOwner`** \u2014 *side-effect*: maps the DTO to an `Owner`; defaults `registrationDate` to today if absent; rolls that date forward to the next business day (skipping weekends and the listed 2026 holidays).\n\n**7. `AssignHouseholdId`** \u2014 *side-effect*: sets `householdId` = first 12 hex of `SHA-256(normalizedLastName + \"|\" + postcode)`.\n\n**8. `CheckHouseholdUnique`** \u2014 *validation*: **409** if that `householdId` already belongs to an existing non-deleted owner \u2014 **unless** the body declared `sharesHousehold: true`, which waives this block (soft-deleted owners don't block).\n\n**9. `CheckOwnerIdentityUnique`** \u2014 *validation*: **409** if the owner's full `identityKey` (`normalizedTelephone|email|householdId`) equals an existing non-deleted owner's.\n\n**10. `AssignHouseholdMemberCount`** \u2014 *side-effect*: sets `householdMemberCount` = existing owners sharing the `householdId`, plus this one.\n\n**11. `AssignNamesakeCount`** \u2014 *side-effect*: sets `namesakeCount` = existing owners sharing this `firstName`+`lastName` (case-insensitive), excluding this one.\n\n**12. `AssignCustomerCode`** \u2014 *side-effect*: sets `customerCode` = `<REGION>-<HASH8>` (REGION from postcode-range then city table then `UNKNOWN`; HASH8 = first 8 upper-hex of `SHA-256(normalizedTelephone + lastName)`), de-duplicated with `-<n>` (n \u2265 2) on collision with an existing code.\n\n**13. `AssignBulkSignupWarning`** \u2014 *side-effect*: sets `bulkSignupWarning = true` when > 80 owners were already created on today's business day.\n\n**14. `AssignPossibleDuplicate`** \u2014 *side-effect*: sets `possibleDuplicate`/`possibleDuplicateOf` when a non-hard-duplicate owner shares this `lastName`+`postcode` but has a different telephone and a different household (earliest matching id wins); otherwise `false`/absent.\n\n**15. `SaveOwner`** \u2014 *side-effect*: persists the owner (generating its id).\n\n**16. `RegisterIdempotency`** \u2014 *side-effect*: records the request's `Idempotency-Key` (if any) against the new owner id, so a later repeat returns this owner.\n\n**17. `AuditOwnerCreated`** \u2014 *side-effect*: writes an `AUDIT` log line with id, customerCode, registrationDate, membershipLevel and membershipNumber.\n\n**18. `RespondWithOwnerCreated`** \u2014 responds **201 Created** with a `Location: /api/owners/{id}` header and the `OwnerDto` body.\n\n### Notes worth flagging\n- The doc-comment on `ValidateOwnerFields` calls itself the \"first step,\" but the YAML actually runs `CheckIdempotencyKey` first; validation is step 2.\n- The capacity/limit checks (steps 4\u20135) and all duplicate checks scan `ownerRepository.findAll()` in memory on every create."
